 "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "2.\tBy the 1920s, automobiles were killing roughly 20,000 Americans per year, the great majority of them children playing in city streets. Newspapers ran front-page lists of the dead with their ages. Cities erected memorials. Several US municipalities seriously considered laws to mechanically limit top speed at the factory. Faced with a mounting regulatory threat that could have crippled their industry, car companies hired publicists, sponsored “safety education” programs in elementary schools, and launched a coordinated nationwide campaign to redefine the city street as a place for vehicles, not people. Central to that campaign was popularizing the term X, a derogatory term adapted from an old American slang word that meant a country bumpkin or rube. Within a decade X had been criminalized across most US cities, and moral responsibility for traffic deaths had been transferred from the driver to the pedestrian. ID X (10 points).", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:39:40Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "And a Creta run over both of them", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:39:56Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Jay", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:39:59Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Jaywalking", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:40:11Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "Answers: X=jaywalking, from jay meaning country bumpkin", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:40:15Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "Jaywalking", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": false, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-22T03:40:38Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "